WEBVTT

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:15.440
My right hand holds a bowl of gold,

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:19.980
And my left holds one of silver.

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:24.520
Never one without the other,

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:37.600
Two unseen bowls for each of us.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:46.010
The golden one is filled with joy,

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:53.350
shining warmly.

00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:58.150
Since we met, my golden bowl

00:00:58.150 --> 00:01:05.160
cannot hold all my happiness and love.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:15.300
Golden joy, silver sadness,

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:22.650
I would leave my past behind...

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:27.380
For you, for the sake of love,

00:01:27.380 --> 00:01:34.320
I would empty the bowls of my past.

00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:01.480
Wait!

00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:05.550
I'm not letting you go. I'm serious.

00:02:05.690 --> 00:02:07.090
I'll kill you if you go.

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:08.890
Pl.. please...

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:12.030
Don't kid with me. What is this?

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:16.630
Wait! Don't go! Please! Wait!

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:28.110
Stop that! Mariko! Come to your senses.

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:31.110
No, I won't let you go! I won't!

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:35.720
Mom, let go of me. Let go! Mom!

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:37.190
Mama! Mama! <b> </b>

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:38.050
Mama! Mama! Mariko!

00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:03.550
So how was Shinobu's birthday party?

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:07.550
Um? ...umm...

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:12.960
Only three people!?!

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:16.690
Mariko, her mother and myself.

00:03:16.690 --> 00:03:18.490
Rich people!

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:21.760
Renting a ball room for a birthday party for three?!?

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:24.570
Usually only two. She and her mom.

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:33.640
So? What happened? <b> </b>

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:34.510
So? What happened? Eh?

00:03:34.910 --> 00:03:37.110
Your expression says, "I'm depressed"

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:40.380
Nothing really. Nothing happened.

00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:45.520
After the party at the hotel, I stopped by her house. That's all.

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:47.390
Oh.. look!

00:03:50.260 --> 00:03:51.390
It's Kaoru-no-Kimi!

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:54.930
Hi!

00:03:57.670 --> 00:04:01.270
Do you run here every weekend?

00:04:01.810 --> 00:04:04.410
No, not usually this far...

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:06.880
...but I'm doing extra training for the district basketball tournament.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:08.410
Bye!

00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:11.150
I'll be there! <b> </b>

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:12.080
I'll be there! Me too!

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:21.690
I can't believe she was hospitalized for a year. She is so energetic!

00:04:21.830 --> 00:04:23.230
I envy her.

00:04:23.230 --> 00:04:23.960
What?

00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:26.030
She's so vibrant!

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:28.100
That's for sure!

00:04:38.510 --> 00:04:39.640
My dear brother...

00:04:40.510 --> 00:04:44.180
That night at Mariko-san's home...

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:45.850
I can't even talk about it to Tomoko.

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:50.450
Tomorrow is Monday.

00:04:50.920 --> 00:04:54.190
How is Mariko-san going to act then?

00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:57.390
I really don't think I can bear seeing her.

00:04:57.790 --> 00:05:03.530
9. Relapse; Broken Heart

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:07.470
Mariko-san...

00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:12.340
Mariko-san! When are you coming out?

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:14.680
Come on, dinner is ready.

00:05:16.610 --> 00:05:17.880
You'll look like a prune!

00:05:21.090 --> 00:05:21.890
Mariko!

00:05:22.750 --> 00:05:23.690
Mariko, you're...

00:05:30.230 --> 00:05:33.560
Mariko, what on earth were you doing?

00:05:35.630 --> 00:05:37.300
Nothing special.

00:05:42.370 --> 00:05:43.840
Good morning! <b> </b>

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:44.780
Good morning! See you later!

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:45.780
Morning! See you later!

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:48.780
Morning!

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:52.580
Good morning!

00:05:53.980 --> 00:05:55.450
See you, Nanako! <b> </b>

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:56.250
See you, Nanako! Sure!

00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:38.100
Good Morning, Nanako-san.

00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:42.230
About the day before yesterday...

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:08.730
During first period and even through second period...

00:07:09.390 --> 00:07:12.930
...I couldn't look at Mariko-san, sitting right next to me.

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:16.530
I couldn't say a word to her.

00:07:17.800 --> 00:07:20.270
Or even breathe.

00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:24.140
I could smell her subtle scent of Rose cologne,

00:07:24.140 --> 00:07:27.680
...and hear her quiet breathing, and my heart sank.

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:35.150
Dear brother... I couldn't forgive her.

00:07:35.290 --> 00:07:37.760
I just couldn't...

00:07:43.360 --> 00:07:44.900
It's going to snow tomorrow. <b> </b>

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:45.500
It's going to snow tomorrow. What?

00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:49.970
This is the first time you asked me to lunch since we entered Seiran.

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:52.500
Is... is that right?

00:07:52.570 --> 00:07:55.370
It is really a pleasure.

00:07:56.170 --> 00:08:00.380
Sometimes, of course, Tora wants to lunch with Tama.

00:08:00.380 --> 00:08:05.250
But Tama is a friend of Mike, and Tora, and everyone else too!

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:10.860
Hey Tama, you don't have much appetite today...

00:08:11.660 --> 00:08:12.460
Meow!

00:08:19.470 --> 00:08:20.800
See you on the way home! <b> </b>

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:22.530
See you on the way home! Goro Nyan!

00:08:30.410 --> 00:08:33.680
There is only one true love for me. Only one.

00:08:34.150 --> 00:08:36.220
She was the world to me!

00:08:36.750 --> 00:08:40.020
Under this shrouded moon, I will jump into the river;

00:08:40.020 --> 00:08:44.760
...with a scream from deep within my heart.

00:08:48.830 --> 00:08:52.900
I am sorry. You are no substitute for her.

00:08:53.900 --> 00:08:58.500
Despite all your beauty and devotion.

00:08:59.510 --> 00:09:02.240
...you cannot fill my emptiness.

00:09:02.710 --> 00:09:03.910
Giovanni-sama!

00:09:05.780 --> 00:09:08.920
Still, my dear, won't you come die with me?

00:09:30.400 --> 00:09:32.070
Kaoru-sama!

00:09:32.810 --> 00:09:35.810
What's wrong? Are you all right?

00:09:37.810 --> 00:09:41.550
Please hold on! Where... where does it hurt?

00:09:43.350 --> 00:09:45.690
What can I do? Help!

00:09:51.490 --> 00:09:52.430
Please...

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:59.100
I need... could you get me some kind of painkiller?

00:09:59.770 --> 00:10:01.030
Painkiller?

00:10:01.170 --> 00:10:09.440
Yes. Go ask Rei. She should have some. Tell her I need it.

00:10:10.510 --> 00:10:12.380
OK... please wait here!

00:10:15.650 --> 00:10:19.320
I'll be in the clubroom. The basketball club.

00:10:19.790 --> 00:10:20.450
OK!

00:10:26.660 --> 00:10:31.000
Dear brother... what's happening to Kaoru-no-Kimi?

00:10:36.070 --> 00:10:40.210
Asaka-san? I don't know... She was here in the morning...

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:41.270
Thank you.

00:10:44.810 --> 00:10:45.610
Maybe...!

00:10:56.420 --> 00:10:57.620
Saint-Juste-sama...

00:11:02.960 --> 00:11:04.570
At the theater.

00:11:05.300 --> 00:11:09.570
Hadn't you heard? She's a guest performer in the play.

00:11:10.040 --> 00:11:12.440
And today the first rehearsal in open to the public.

00:11:20.710 --> 00:11:22.450
Wow! We got to come see it.

00:11:26.050 --> 00:11:27.450
Thank you very much.

00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:29.520
This will definitely be a success. <b> </b>

00:11:29.520 --> 00:11:30.190
This will definitely be a success. Sure, bye!

00:11:35.860 --> 00:11:37.060
Please take these flowers.

00:11:37.600 --> 00:11:40.270
I was moved to tears! I won't be able to sleep tonight!

00:11:40.270 --> 00:11:42.870
It was no big deal. I messed up three of my lines.

00:11:43.400 --> 00:11:45.740
Saint Juste-sama! It's Kaoru-no-Kimi!

00:11:47.070 --> 00:11:48.140
Saint Juste-sama!

00:11:48.880 --> 00:11:50.880
Please, please let me through.

00:11:51.280 --> 00:11:53.610
Who're you... cut it out!

00:11:54.150 --> 00:11:55.220
Saint Juste-sama!

00:11:55.280 --> 00:11:58.690
Oh... she's the one who tricked her way into the Sorority...

00:11:58.820 --> 00:12:00.220
Get lost!

00:12:17.100 --> 00:12:19.640
It makes no difference with whom I die.

00:12:21.640 --> 00:12:23.850
The cold wind blows through my soul.

00:12:37.660 --> 00:12:41.800
Kaoru-no-Kimi is asking for a painkiller! Please give her one of yours!

00:12:42.660 --> 00:12:46.870
Soon to end my life, I look up from the river's side...

00:12:47.740 --> 00:12:52.270
...and see a single streak of cloud over a celebrating moon.

00:12:53.140 --> 00:12:56.880
Strange insects buzz around my ears, and fireflies...

00:12:58.210 --> 00:12:59.550
Saint Juste-sama!

00:13:01.880 --> 00:13:06.090
This icy water will be the last warmth I feel during my final moments.

00:13:06.690 --> 00:13:10.090
Kaoru-no-Kimi needs it. She's suffering!

00:13:10.890 --> 00:13:12.360
Won't you die with me?

00:13:16.360 --> 00:13:18.030
How can you laugh?!

00:13:28.510 --> 00:13:32.180
What's so funny! Our friend is suffering!

00:13:32.450 --> 00:13:33.650
Please give it to me!

00:13:42.320 --> 00:13:43.990
Ma cherie La Poupee...

00:13:49.060 --> 00:13:50.530
Ma cherie La Poupee...

00:13:51.870 --> 00:13:53.070
A painkiller, you say?

00:13:54.140 --> 00:13:57.070
Well these are tranquilizers, here...

00:13:58.140 --> 00:14:01.010
...and a hematogenic, and vitamins...

00:14:01.010 --> 00:14:03.010
Ah, found it. Here they are.

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:10.690
Tell her not to take too many...

00:14:12.290 --> 00:14:13.890
Th... thank you!

00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:26.100
Ma cherie La Poupee, my dear Poupee, who slapped me...

00:14:29.840 --> 00:14:32.840
Drugs... and more drugs.

00:14:33.980 --> 00:14:35.780
Saint Juste-sama is drenched in drugs...!

00:14:37.450 --> 00:14:38.650
Excuse me, I'm going now...

00:14:39.050 --> 00:14:41.050
Bye, see you later...

00:14:48.520 --> 00:14:52.130
She asked for a painkiller. Is it that serious?

00:15:12.950 --> 00:15:14.020
Thanks.

00:15:14.620 --> 00:15:16.820
I'll be fine. Very soon.

00:15:18.090 --> 00:15:20.620
You should go. Afternoon classes are starting.

00:15:21.560 --> 00:15:22.430
But...

00:15:22.960 --> 00:15:25.490
I will be resting here for a while.

00:15:28.430 --> 00:15:29.970
I will stay right here!

00:15:31.630 --> 00:15:33.170
Don't worry, silly.

00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:36.510
I'm still recovering, like I said before.

00:15:37.710 --> 00:15:38.780
Please let me stay!

00:15:39.440 --> 00:15:43.180
You're more stubborn than you look. OK then, but only for fifth period.

00:15:43.710 --> 00:15:44.250
OK!

00:15:44.780 --> 00:15:45.720
What a fuss!

00:15:57.530 --> 00:15:58.530
How about sports?

00:15:59.130 --> 00:16:01.330
Were you in any sports clubs in junior high?

00:16:01.800 --> 00:16:03.330
Nothing in particular...

00:16:04.200 --> 00:16:06.000
I'm not talented at sports.

00:16:07.070 --> 00:16:10.210
But the ones I like are tennis, swimming and basketball.

00:16:10.740 --> 00:16:11.740
I see.

00:16:12.540 --> 00:16:15.280
But talent doesn't matter.

00:16:15.680 --> 00:16:18.350
But I'm so ordinary!

00:16:21.550 --> 00:16:23.490
What's funny?

00:16:26.960 --> 00:16:29.430
I was hospitalized for a long time, remember?

00:16:30.230 --> 00:16:31.160
Yes.

00:16:31.630 --> 00:16:35.230
Now... I have a craving...

00:16:36.170 --> 00:16:39.900
...to run very hard... up to the limit.

00:16:42.040 --> 00:16:43.710
Until my heart... bursts.

00:16:46.380 --> 00:16:47.710
My heartbeats...

00:16:48.180 --> 00:16:53.380
I can hear them like music, cheerful and happy...

00:16:54.790 --> 00:16:58.920
It made me realize that just ordinary living is a great thing.

00:17:00.260 --> 00:17:03.460
...and I feel great...

00:17:03.530 --> 00:17:07.200
...and run some more...

00:17:07.260 --> 00:17:08.730
...and chase the ball...

00:17:13.140 --> 00:17:17.140
Now, I feel much better.

00:17:19.740 --> 00:17:20.680
That's good.

00:17:21.480 --> 00:17:24.750
Can you come wake me up, after sixth period?

00:17:25.420 --> 00:17:30.020
Feeling drowsy like this, I may fall asleep...

00:17:31.290 --> 00:17:32.690
Yes, of course!

00:17:33.620 --> 00:17:37.560
[Our hopes were too quickly drained there.]

00:17:37.560 --> 00:17:42.630
[The sights during that time and the group's decisions were such that we reported them.] <b> </b> <b> </b>

00:17:42.630 --> 00:17:45.840
[The sights during that time and the group's decisions were such that we reported them.] Dear Brother, during sixth period that day...

00:17:45.840 --> 00:17:46.970
Dear Brother, during sixth period that day...

00:17:46.970 --> 00:17:48.110
[At first we thought that...] Dear Brother, during sixth period that day...

00:17:48.110 --> 00:17:48.440
[At first we thought that...] <b> </b> <b> </b>

00:17:48.440 --> 00:17:50.510
[At first we thought that...] ...I was in another world, removed from both school and Mariko-san.

00:17:50.510 --> 00:17:54.110
...I was in another world, removed from both school and Mariko-san.

00:17:54.980 --> 00:17:59.180
I was worrying that whole time,

00:17:59.180 --> 00:18:03.920
...worrying that she might wake up in the clubroom, alone, and in pain.

00:18:25.480 --> 00:18:28.010
Oh, excuse me... where is Kaoru-no-Kimi?

00:18:28.410 --> 00:18:29.610
She left early.

00:18:29.880 --> 00:18:31.080
Left early?

00:18:31.080 --> 00:18:35.420
She left a note saying "I will be leaving early today".

00:18:36.090 --> 00:18:38.020
I... I see...

00:18:45.830 --> 00:18:48.100
She must have had a relapse then!

00:18:48.100 --> 00:18:52.700
So then... I should get her phone number from the office and call her!

00:19:08.520 --> 00:19:10.520
Excuse me, listen, Nanako-chan...

00:19:10.920 --> 00:19:13.390
I need to say something, it's important.

00:19:14.530 --> 00:19:16.730
Sorry! I'm in a hurry!

00:19:39.820 --> 00:19:45.290
Many times, Dear Brother, so many times I called...

00:19:46.360 --> 00:19:48.160
...using the number I got from the school office.

00:19:49.030 --> 00:19:50.760
That was all I could do.

00:19:51.960 --> 00:19:54.700
And even if she answered the phone,

00:19:54.700 --> 00:19:56.700
I knew I still couldn't really do anything for her.

00:19:56.700 --> 00:19:59.970
Hanging up the phone would just make me worry more.

00:20:01.040 --> 00:20:05.580
There was no answer, and I didn't know what else to do.

00:20:09.250 --> 00:20:12.580
Finally, I stopped trying.

00:20:15.790 --> 00:20:20.390
No one understands. Nobody truly understands another.

00:20:21.460 --> 00:20:24.800
But someone who cares can still try.

00:20:27.330 --> 00:20:30.140
Does that mean that even if we worry about others,

00:20:31.140 --> 00:20:36.340
...there is nothing we can really do for them?

00:20:36.880 --> 00:20:38.410
Is that what you mean?

00:20:51.090 --> 00:20:53.230
Doctor, thank you for your time.

00:20:54.090 --> 00:20:56.630
She came here today, didn't she?

00:21:01.570 --> 00:21:05.700
Yes, but not for a routine check up; she said she had a sudden pain.

00:21:06.040 --> 00:21:07.970
And? How bad is it?

00:21:08.170 --> 00:21:11.510
Don't worry. Don't concern yourself.

00:21:11.910 --> 00:21:13.450
This sort of thing happens.

00:21:13.580 --> 00:21:15.650
I see. Thank goodness.

00:21:15.920 --> 00:21:21.990
The pain is gone, and she said she was off to a night practice at school.

00:21:22.520 --> 00:21:23.860
Thank you so much.

00:21:24.520 --> 00:21:27.790
It's good that she plays basketball.

00:21:29.200 --> 00:21:32.730
What does that mean? You mean, while she can?

00:21:34.200 --> 00:21:36.340
Don't say such stupid things!

00:21:38.200 --> 00:21:40.070
I'm sorry...

00:22:08.900 --> 00:22:10.900
Please, won't someone explain to me...

00:22:12.040 --> 00:22:16.180
What is the point of our being born and living?

00:22:26.790 --> 00:22:29.860
No one truly understands another.

00:22:31.790 --> 00:22:33.990
I cannot feel her chest pain,

00:22:34.460 --> 00:22:39.930
So the seriousness of her illness, and what that illness is, I can't know.

00:22:41.740 --> 00:22:44.870
...because no one can truly understand another.

00:22:46.870 --> 00:22:48.610
But, brother...

00:22:49.940 --> 00:22:53.550
...if someone so alive and vibrant...

00:22:53.750 --> 00:22:57.080
...has such a sadness and a dark side...

00:22:57.820 --> 00:23:01.890
She, the very last person I would have guessed...

00:23:11.230 --> 00:23:13.970
I cannot bear the thought!

00:23:24.440 --> 00:23:28.850
Here, Mariko-san. You should eat...

00:23:34.590 --> 00:23:35.920
Go ahead, Mariko...

00:23:36.390 --> 00:23:38.190
Keep the hell out of my life !!

00:23:42.600 --> 00:23:43.460
Mariko!

00:24:09.960 --> 00:24:14.160
I dreamed I was chasing a rainbow...

00:24:14.160 --> 00:24:19.630
Then the rainbow I was chasing was you.

00:24:21.100 --> 00:24:25.240
Before, I had no strength, no will.

00:24:25.240 --> 00:24:30.710
But now because of you, I do.

00:24:31.450 --> 00:24:36.980
Feelings of love, like raindrops

00:24:36.980 --> 00:24:42.460
Come pouring from the sky.

00:24:42.460 --> 00:24:45.190
This is surely a game

00:24:45.190 --> 00:24:48.000
Of some mischievous fairy...

00:24:48.000 --> 00:24:50.400
Always dancing,

00:24:50.400 --> 00:24:55.670
Always capricious...

00:25:01.680 --> 00:25:03.540
Preview

00:25:03.540 --> 00:25:06.350
Nanako continues to shun Mariko.

00:25:06.950 --> 00:25:11.550
One day, Mariko suddenly faints while at school.

00:25:12.090 --> 00:25:15.290
When Nanako goes to Mariko's house to let her mother know,

00:25:15.690 --> 00:25:18.960
Nanako learns about Mariko's shocking secret.

00:25:19.690 --> 00:25:20.700
Next episode: <b> </b>

00:25:20.700 --> 00:25:21.960
Next episode: Mariko

00:25:22.100 --> 00:25:23.630
Brother, Dear Brother... <b> </b>

00:25:23.630 --> 00:25:29.700
Brother, Dear Brother... There is no end to my tears...
